# Git promotion (local → dev → prod)

Order is **local commit → push to the named dev remote/branch → promote to prod**. Cursor may **ask** whether to push. It must not push, deploy, or apply SQL to **dev** or **prod** until the user names that target in this turn.

## Allowed without extra approval

- Edit files, run local tests, `git status` / `git diff` / `git log`.
- **Commit** only when the user asks to commit (existing commit protocol).
- **Ask:** “Commit locally?” / “Push this SHA to **dev**?” / “Promote this SHA to **prod**?”

## Forbidden unless the user names the environment this turn

- `git push` (any remote, including `origin`, `dev`, `prod`)
- `gh` create/merge that updates a protected remote
- Vercel / Docker / host deploy to a named env
- `CONFIRM_APPLY=1` or any migration runner against a named Supabase project other than the one they named

“Looks good”, “ship it”, or finishing a ROADMAP chunk is **not** push approval. They must say **dev** or **prod** (or the remote/project URL).

Local `.env` stays on DEV `https://cmksomahsfmsjufakryw.supabase.co`. Do not retarget `.env` to another project to “help”.

